course: dictionary
lesson: 10875
title: Roman numerals: VIII
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: VIII is a Roman numeral, a way of writing numbers with letters. In «Henry VIII was tall, strong and sporty as a young king», the word VIII is not a word to sound out. It is a number, and the clue is the name Henry: kings are often numbered, so VIII means the eighth King Henry.
explain: Roman numerals add up the letters. V means 5 and I means 1, so VIII is V plus three I's: 5 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 8. Try it in the sentence: «The woman shouts "Stop, stop, stop!" in chapter VIII» makes sense if VIII is a chapter number, which is what the words around it suggest.
explain: Where might you see VIII? In a history book, in a king's name. In a book, at the start of a chapter. On a clock face, as an hour. Use the clues around the word to work out which one you are reading. When you are not sure, ask: does a number fit here?
fact: VIII is the Roman numeral for 8.
fact: VIII is V (5) followed by three I's (1 + 1 + 1), so 5 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 8.
fact: «Henry VIII» was an English king who had six wives.
fact: Roman numerals are used for kings' names, chapter numbers and the hours on some clock faces.
exercise: What number does the Roman numeral VIII stand for? | 5 | 3 | *8 | 18
exercise: In «Henry VIII was tall, strong and sporty as a young king», what does VIII show? | The king's age | A kind of horse | The year he was born | *The number of the king: Henry the eighth
exercise: Which sum makes VIII? | *5 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 8 | 5 + 5 + 1 = 11 | 10 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 13 | 1 + 1 = 2
test: On a Roman numeral clock, the hour hand points at VIII. What time is it? | 12 o'clock | *8 o'clock | 9 o'clock | 6 o'clock
test: «...just as the policemen on the engine shouted in chapter VIII.» Which chapter number is VIII? | *8 | 5 | 3 | 18
exam: Which Roman numeral means 8? | VII | VI | *VIII | IX
